<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">South African Communist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SACP, Communist Party of South Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South African Communist Party was founded in 1921 as the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, banned in 1950 and re-formed underground in 1953. Closely allied with the ANC, it co-founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umkhonto-we-sizwe">Umkhonto we Sizwe</a> and supplied many leaders of the liberation struggle, including Joe Slovo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chris-hani">Chris Hani</a>. It was unbanned in 1990 and remains part of the ANC-led governing alliance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-african-communist-party.jpg" alt="South African Communist Party" width="320" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MrPenguin20 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_South_African_Communist_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
